# Backend Hardening & TDD Guide

Pause feature work to install a test harness and harden the backend before resuming Lesson 12. This guide replaces "go straight to converter resolver UI" with a 6-phase pass that pays for itself across every subsequent feature.

## How to use this guide

- One phase per session. Don't combine. Context drift is real on this project.
- Every phase ends at a clean commit point. Don't move on without it.
- Steps are checkboxes — tick them as you go.
- Code blocks are reference material, not full implementations. Adapt to the actual files you have open.

## Phase order

- [ ] **[00 — Prerequisites](./part-1)** — Three blocking fixes before any test work
- [ ] **[01 — Phase A: Test Infrastructure](./part-2)** — Rollback fixture, ASGI client, smoke tests
- [ ] **[02 — Phase B: Pure Unit Tests](./part-3)** — Converter, price helper, banker's-rounding bugs
- [ ] **[03 — Phase C: Service Integration](./part-4)** — Scryfall sync hardening, idempotency, retries
- [ ] **[04 — Phase D: Resolver & GraphQL Tests](./part-5)** — `schema.execute()`, typed-error Unions, N+1 guards
- [ ] **[05 — Phase E: Hardening Pass](./part-6)** — MaskErrors, structlog, UNIQUE constraints, lazy="raise_on_sql"
- [ ] **[06 — Phase F: Final Smoke Pass](./part-7)** — Random-seed run, coverage review, mypy strict, ship it

## Top-line decisions (locked)

- **pytest-asyncio 1.x in `auto` mode** with session-scoped event loop
- **`join_transaction_mode="create_savepoint"`** for per-test rollback isolation
- **`schema.execute()`** for ~80% of resolver tests; `httpx.AsyncClient` + `ASGITransport` for the wiring layer
- **respx** for Scryfall/EDHRec mocking; static fixture JSON for parser tests
- **structlog + asgi-correlation-id** for logging
- **Typed-error Unions** for expected GraphQL failures; **`MaskErrors`** extension for unexpected ones
- **Skip testcontainers** — add `mtg_test` to existing Compose Postgres
- **Skip pytest-xdist** — not needed at this suite size

## Known bugs the test suite should land on

These are confirmed in the codebase. Don't fix them out of order — write the failing test first, then fix.

- `_price_cents` uses `round()` (banker's rounding): `round(0.5) == 0`, so `"0.005"` → `0` cents instead of `1`
- `_card_to_row` uses `round(cmc)`: cards with `cmc=0.5` (Little Girl) silently become `cmc=0`
- Scryfall sync commits per batch — partial failure leaves up to 499 cards committed with no rollback
- `on_conflict_do_update` `set_` dict omits `updated_at` — re-syncs never refresh the timestamp
- `httpx.AsyncClient` has no retry transport, no `User-Agent` header
- `CollectionItem` has no UNIQUE on `(scryfall_id, foil, condition, language)` — concurrent adds create duplicates
- `add_to_collection` has no FK existence check before insert

## Estimated effort

8–14 working days end-to-end, heavily front-loaded on Phase A. The harness is the single most leveraged piece of work — Phases B–F are mostly mechanical once it's right.
